diffs.patch:
Index: openwiki/.claims/architecture/frontend.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/architecture/frontend.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/architecture/frontend.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:e2a153dd9a30df23916b9143b1d58d851795dc01e156c370da218011d7f4528a",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0ec55d29a4cf41bfb773f6e4e39ee67f",
+      "statement": "The frontend is a pure single-page application that holds no authoritative state; all of its knowledge and changes go through the RPC API defined in packages/workshop-shared (src/api.ts).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/api.ts#L1-L24",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1838e0177eaeb013e44ab9374d4b1ff3908cac932a0bc81b00a86f85fc85f87e:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_458a3a3e0c9b46899b6eea8e0d6cf83c",
+      "statement": "The app opens one persistent Cap'n Web WebSocket RPC session to the backend at startup and reconnects on loss; connection management is hoisted into module-level globals in src/main.tsx rather than React state to avoid duplicate sockets in dev-effect double runs.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/src/main.tsx#L47-L108",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:62aee1c999fd70bfa238a0dee71d4bf1dd8c3f9e01cf022bd2146cf5d2a0e436:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8a1645671f2b42cc88760e5e8b8f0f0b",
+      "statement": "On RPC loss the frontend immediately publishes a new RpcPromise wrapping reconnect(), so calls pipelined during the outage are queued and delivered in order once the replacement connection is proven with a ping(), instead of failing against a dead socket.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/src/main.tsx#L107-L153",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:108469fa003c272f6c0e721d844e0ff34caeeabd70ac59d681317cf5d6684c29:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ddaace68ad174d0fa1d4f4ff340df862",
+      "statement": "The frontend intentionally pipelines the returned AuthenticatedApi stub into React state rather than awaiting it: both authenticate(token) and authenticateFromCfAccess() are used as stubs immediately, with auth errors surfacing when the stub is used.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/src/useAuth.ts#L96-L119",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:07f0d85844e13f5a17f4cc880e6120e57726ad5088084ecbccde06e3931a8dcb:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_08841ba8b3f2464d81ad152bba514761",
+      "statement": "Gadget UIs run in sandboxed iframes whose only communication channel is postMessage() to the parent, over which they speak Cap'n Web RPC; the injected caller imports a nested data: URL copy of capnwebhare to set up the MessagePort session.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/src/GadgetUI.tsx#L10-L33",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:50adf2dc757493ff5f1faa72e3fd9f393bcb360ec03b7464acaca172302aa370:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/src/GadgetUI.tsx#L105-L116",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:75811c2a413cb90401b91808266ee271b8bb915bd68f8675a2f1033263a0b915:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_219e76bbcbbb4e83898141de3fd783f1",
+      "statement": "Gatekeeper management apps are hosted by SandboxedGatekeeperApp in a network-isolated srcDoc iframe with srctl origin, reaching the gatekeeper through the Workshop-relayed and rate-limited ui capability.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/src/SandboxedGatekeeperApp.tsx#L301-L373",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eb94509168ccc86687a3a1a952a0e0289cbd7ce3e72d56ffd95cf877e158a30d:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/src/SandboxedGatekeeperApp.tsx#L81-L119",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:79aec1930f7f20b39d86df47c7cc7bf3bc614ca645986b51c7f76af4a15daf25:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_05e7db7830a248d8a02ccafb06c10d69",
+      "statement": "The frontend selects between password and Cloudflare Access auth modes at build time: VITE_CF_ACCESS_MODE=true disables the login/signup pages and authenticates via authenticateFromCfAccess().",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/README.md#L21-L48",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eeb5a627351a41a0dd91fd11bd9c4f7230e26b06367c923bbddfb8004ca6a938:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0dd88c9b2e984641b0b852fac55b0a1f",
+      "statement": "The frontend build is a Vite+ task declaring env: ['VITE_*'] so Vite flags are fingerprinted into the task cache, always produces a production bundle, and deletes dist/ before building so a cache hit cannot leave stale sourcemaps.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/README.md#L13-L19",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e0ae0e6df64de78592a8965db49a0337c4627598d7be8ccdf05f7b67f5d38d1f:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-12T21:03:26.424Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/architecture/overview.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/architecture/overview.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/architecture/overview.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:6fe532693f99f03e1dfe834c6d2547f1561edb8a4581d36ab945ee5798f2daac",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_892a952b37534adc8bc394f8fdba13d5",
+      "statement": "The repo maps an OS analogy onto packages: workshop-backend is the kernel, gatekeeper-* are device drivers, workshop-frontend is the shell, gadgets are processes, blueprints are executables, and AI agents are treated as actors that must be accountable to a human yet have their own restricted permissions.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L95-L112",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7fdb1f9b58bdd6613c2f8e58994362dad480767d1bd4b9573e688ad809705e42:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_49141313020a4186a0882a7ce868b7ef",
+      "statement": "everything in the system communicates over Cap'n Web RPC: the client/server interface in packages/workshop-shared/src/api.ts, gatekeeper/Workshop RPC, and gadget/Workshop RPC over postMessage in a sandboxed iframe.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/api.ts#L1-L24",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1838e0177eaeb013e44ab9374d4b1ff3908cac932a0bc81b00a86f85fc85f87e:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_cdae7a875ddc4d36b6a3df6d9ff76205",
+      "statement": "The public origin is packages/router, which dispatches purely by path prefix: /gatekeeper/<name>/* to whatever GATEKEEPER_* service binding is present (so installing a gatekeeper is a binding change), /api/* and /blueprint-screenshot/* to workshop-backend, and everything else to the frontend assets.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/router/src/index.ts#L24-L59",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8b96dc25e68d850277c0ddb9edbfc29e751a4353291acbf0d7101e0311a3601c:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_e0a201b6082145538a19c591d8dd8385",
+      "statement": "every workspace is its own Durable Object and every gadget runs in a Dynamic Worker Facet; the backend wrangler.jsonc declares the UserDurableObject, OverseerDurableObject, AdminSettings, and PendingLogin Durable Object classes plus BLUEPRINTS/AVATARS KV namespaces and the BLUEPRINT_CONTENT R2 bucket.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/wrangler.jsonc#L1-L79",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ac4c6bb4bf22804f3de6cdf8aa3c93c394f195a38114879728f68d684508a1df:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_927b01cbb5fc459fb8a5ddb267194654",
+      "statement": "agents and gadgets by default have access to nothing; the user must introduce each agent/gadget to any resource it needs, rather than MCP servers being configured upfront for ambient access.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L164-L170",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9b052069f5eeca8bb6e41afc3fcd8e960b7e1f522dbb254b9bc347c4c3b6e84c:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-12T21:03:26.424Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/architecture/shared-api.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/architecture/shared-api.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/architecture/shared-api.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:59c013feea2fa29cae8b9239fe22b769f7d78700870ac2d718e9d08664edf3b4",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_89e0b04cc7334e73b4c0b184016e7c69",
+      "statement": "The RPC API is a hierarchy of Cap'n Web capability interfaces in workshops-shared: PublicApi (unauthenticated), AuthenticatedApi (signed-in user), and Overseer (per-workspace, returned by openGadget/newGadget), all spoken over a persistent WebSocket the client reconnects as needed.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/api.ts#L1-L24",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1838e0177eaeb013e44ab9374d4b1ff3908cac932a0bc81b00a86f85fc85f87e:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/api.ts#L360-L360",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e6b6df9c7e2578f69216e7467ac41c30e745943e5812c92bf0675f2617a37059:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_450c98455a144a8d977356c3327f7a5c",
+      "statement": "Admin capability is minted once by getAdminApi() which performs the access check at mint time, so the returned AdminApi stub's methods need no per-call authorization checks, and a compromised admin session cannot use it to change auth config which stays env-var driven.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/api.ts#L706-L712",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:db268ce3a4d830f16dd644893fb1618838ae947d41b10c82fddc969cb9ad97f5:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9cbad70759ed45ec85eeab1c424dec7a",
+      "statement": "Expected failures carry stable machine-readable error codes built by a codedErrorFamily helper; the per-code messages double as the classification fallback for errors from older deployments that lost the code in transit, so changing a message is a compatibility break.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/api.ts#L301-L352",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:54a7a56134fba792ff55a0cb3c44416004e39a1301ccf158986fc80c95215995:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0db8f9c24d994bafa5ff3daa5b012ac9",
+      "statement": "validateBindingName() is the single shared validator applied at every chokepoint that writes a binding name; it rejects non-JS-identifiers, reserved words, and property names colliding with Object.prototype members.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/api.ts#L177-L220",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7c1aec592438c19dd43b541134c71d3e118bbf80b9e009b0892ef49b836d291d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_b0e6f541d7c3493eb9fcecbd466bd77a",
+      "statement": "code-change.ts is the single owner of the operational-transform representation of uncommitted code changes (wire types, application, composition, transformation, diffing, ingestion validation, and the priority convention), with the text-OT core being @codemirror/state's ChangeSet and change generation using fast-diff.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/code-change.ts#L14-L55",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b26e7da1912753daf4471f86ad5d7fdd87950c23bc5dcafa94ccdcf2e27902f6:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_94b7ef59566a4e60a56cd1d356973f3b",
+      "statement": "A CodeChange maps each gadget to a list of [path, FileChange] entries rather than a path-keyed object, because file paths can be any non-empty string including names that collide with Object.prototype and would be silently deleted by Cap'n Web's prototype-shadowing key handling.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/code-change.ts#L80-L98",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bb06961f2fb8e07af1f670ec41c4e43d82897d324b93a24a9c339acdc9f3c8e0:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_bf227f1e36a740b4b40ac074befdcb5d",
+      "statement": "RPC edge types are established by capnweb-validate at the boundary; validation stages check invariants a TS type cannot express rather than re-checking structural validity.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/code-change.ts#L45-L55",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:900d3902602477ae80aa854d83519b82e37443df6f24817731741d9df92525a4:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-12T21:03:26.424Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/architecture/the-gate-by-model.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/architecture/the-gate-by-model.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/architecture/the-gate-by-model.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,118 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:84972616bc9e551871d822f94feaf4ebbcaf9c0e7e0f490dbaf1034e5b5e4a66",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_52636dc380cf4644aa5b1027136b88d1",
+      "statement": "A gatekeeper exposes a hierarchy of RPC capabilities: GatekeeperVendor (the service binding), GatekeeperUser (a connected account, 'already specialized for a particular human user', which only the Workshop itself may hold), and Gatekeeper<Session> (a per-resource binding executed as a Durable Object Facet under the Overseer).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L445-L445",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b2eb1c76a7fd5f46fe594d110865a2e6b3e869ae8e9a63182cc435ce97723e66:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L567-L567",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:01203c694fb82122413fb9a2b6582686dd73f003b4b9d6ceb6ac2d59950e3ea1:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L698-L698",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a15b3d46b9afe05fa91111220f68a3940ccf81f3241dabab8efd3cb0d44b67af:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c636afa5fbfa4f7eba33edaeafc7bf22",
+      "statement": "In the approval-queue model, observations (authorizeObservation) are read-only and the gatekeeper must wait for authorization before returning data, while actions (submitAction) are fully asynchronous and only actually carried out when applyAction() is eventually called — so a user can approve queued actions in bulk, possibly hours or days later.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L934-L957",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f6e977dd91a656bdaeca50825fe3d50649228cdf176a67a92ade2370417910d6:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c9bbbd248d5c4184b69ac66ded5af593",
+      "statement": "A gatekeeper is expected to simulate unapproved actions so the Session reflects state as if all actions had applied, letting the gadget queue more dependent actions; rejectAction may signal restart when an accepted simulation cannot be rolled back cleanly.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L731-L829",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:91f90d2a629b3e9bf9f5b42876e407a34a466273eda6185ba047e5635855d712:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_4ad90e9dec3449c1a78f4681a7314600",
+      "statement": "Gatekeeper.addObserver(id, verifier) must throw if the user is not allowed to observe everything read through the gatekeeper so far; otherwise the gatekeeper remembers the observer and future observations set excludeObservers to name who must not see them, and removeObserver must be idempotent.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L753-L795",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4647a324684782e5d5bf8181f1322d696154438a5d2a545bf34f04b636812d5b:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_440e5725ed734c83a54f62b0eac4e297",
+      "statement": "The verifier pattern is that GatekeeperUserVerifier implements a public-but-non-standard method its own gatekeeper's addObserver can call and trust, valid because the overseer promises to return a verifier only to the gatekeeper that minted it.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L675-L689",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d6b1989d16f98c28de36816f2667d9c967af01069a7a71a4e7c56f0b1e7b2d34:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_498cfc28965b4bcea1c96398acf386a7",
+      "statement": "GatekeeperVendor.createAccount() mints a new connected account with no OAuth flow and is safe on the public interface only because it takes no user identity; the resulting account capability is the authority thereafter.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L514-L523",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e906c160c5d0e8be5c1d679c2cde12a1d5097a5d7252b3860b712e34090d5475:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c358856584f748c8958f9b281cbf39df",
+      "statement": "Auto-provisioning of ambient gatekeepers is a deployment admin three-state mode (disabled / optional / enabled, default optional), resolved in provisioning-policy.ts which is the single chokepoint the UserDurableObject calls; enabled forces the account for every user, disabled leaves existing accounts dormant.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/provisioning-policy.ts#L14-L34",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8c23efb6bd3a16cac0949b3741e62d7bd0b9798311da7ea46280dc304d239a08:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_5033f759200a49999d409fb378134498",
+      "statement": "GatekeeperConnectOptions distinguishes scopes 'auth' (minimal email-verification scopes, transient grant discarded after getAuthenticatedEmail) from 'full' (capability scopes, persisted), and resourceUrlPatterns:[] is meaningful and distinct from omitting it (it requests no resource authorization).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L440-L478",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fadba32e4ea77a3451b216aa4320e745c45405ae38b28404b22457ee32e8f945:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_3d760f07888a42488ec35b46dfddd8b7",
+      "statement": "resolveRequestedResource is the single source of truth shared by backend and frontend for which resource an agent connection request pre-selects, returning a human-readable reason rather than opening an empty pre-selection when none applies.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L301-L345",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4171862bdeb2c2678943508592c867b0adba3d039c4e25c9818bc5da37150e9f:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_01d16160ddb94fe5b86474c56e21510a",
+      "statement": "getAgentCatalog returns bounded discovery metadata whose access is an observation; boundAgentCatalog enforces hard caps (1000 entries; 256/100/400-char id/title/description) because the catalog is injected into the agent as untrusted data, and the Workshop re-clamps what it receives.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L94-L145",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5af4acefb66d8526065210fd50d2924ae5bce4b4836eea1a651c298d141a3564:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-12T21:03:26.424Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/concepts/gadget-lifecycle.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/concepts/gadget-lifecycle.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/concepts/gadget-lifecycle.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,88 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:08bfaf034e916e0949cd5fbf33e9bdd5c1bc4b15525d68b81915ec006548fe95",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d4148ed8a57d46a8b4c3ae4e53a28461",
+      "statement": "A gadget is provisional until it has activity such as a chat message or code edit; provisional gadgets are hidden from the home page and automatically deleted after some time, and calling new*Gatekeeper() does not clear the provisional bit unless the gatekeeper is bound into a gadget.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/api.ts",
+          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:a0f0e808353927031a6a79c783a1c753989a26482457edc9b98aabb04721a9ed"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
